{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405871-mages-and-the-penumbra-s","id":1405871,"title":"Mages and the Penumbra(s)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-01T20:08:28-07:00","id":1405871,"title":"Mages and the Penumbra(s)","content":"Hi. I have a question about the Penumbra. According to M20:<br /> <br /> &quot;Here\u2019s an important reminder: the High, Middle, and Low Penumbrae are all the same place. The differences between them don\u2019t reflect the Penumbra itself \u2013 they reflect the travelers who go there&quot; - p.95<br /> <br /> I've had a terrible time trying to swallow this. I find difficult to believe the same place they describe in Wraith as the shadowlands (Wraiths penumbra, if I understand correctly, not an expert on than line), is the same Penumbra werewolves go to. And as far as I get from that paragraph, thats what M20 is telling me. <br /> <br /> How do you guys manage that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:49:30-07:00","id":1405935,"title":"","content":"Easy, I throw out everything from other game lines and run what's in just the mage book since it's a mage centric game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T15:16:01-07:00","id":1406007,"title":"","content":"^ That.<br /> <br /> In a Mage game, the Shadowlands are just the lower aspect of the Penumbra. There is no problem with Wraiths and Werewolfs both being in it.<br /> Also your question kind of doesn't have much to do with Mages per se.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To elaborate, the usual consensus (heh) is that the gameline you're actually running should have priority over all other rules of the gameline(s) you add/shoehorn in. So in a game, &lt;Main gameline's&gt; rules are highest priority. Then come the other gamelines you add, as long as their rules don't contradict &lt;Main gamenile's&gt; rules. And in case things are not obvious or even contradictiory, it's a pure ST decision on how to handle it. As I said..I don't see a problem with weres and wraiths occupying the penumbra. It just sounds like..WoD to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-02-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T18:31:00-07:00","id":1406029,"title":"","content":"Ok, yes, lets suppose I throw away all the other lines. Still, I need to go back to my question: <b>how do you guys manage that (three different ways of perceiving things at once)? </b><br /> <br /> Lets say, you have 3 mages, all of them with different <i>Vidares </i>and you send them to the Penumbra. <br /> <br /> That means, one is seeing the Penumbra the way its described in Werewolf, another one sees it the way described in Wraith, and the third one...well, I already have trouble imagining the Astral Penumbra, but for the sake of argument, lets say she does see it that way (whatever it is). <b>Do you describe things in 3 different ways, one for each vision?</b><br /> <br /> Now, a ghost shows up. <b>Would they see the ghost the same way?</b> I would think that, if they see the Penumbra different - the whole surrounding - they should see the spirits different too. It sounds logical to me.<br /> <br /> My other option would be to throw away the whole <i>Vidare </i>thing and stick to the way they ran it in Revised (which is unknown to me). By any chance, would the Book of Worlds or Infinite Tapestry help me clarify that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T20:18:13-07:00","id":1406046,"title":"","content":"The Astral Penumbra is the High Umbra, or realm of ideals. So, it would be very much driven by thought. Think of concepts--and I doubt they would see a ghost that showed up the same way.<br /> <br /> I would recommend Beyond The Barrier: The Book of Worlds over Infinite Tapestry which I would recommend over having 3 different Penumbras for 3 different mages.<br /> <br /> Beyond The Barrier: The Book of Worlds is pre-Avatar Storm, but you get a lot of evocative locations and the High Umbra, Middle Umbra and Low Umbra are all clearer. Plus, you get all the shade realms for the spheres. Infinite Tapestry is post-Avatar Storm and has a lot of evocative locations, but it's more jumbled and you don't get all the cool spaceships of the Sons of Ether and the Void Engineers fighting. I mix those two with what worked best--for example the last big adventure was to the River of Languages. Book of Worlds wasn't that detailed on it while Infinite Tapestry had a few details on the River of Languages and made it clearer the benefits of drinking from it as well as having stats for River pirates.<br /> <br /> Mage cosmology is pretty out there, so if the other game lines conflict, throw out what doesn't work for your chronicle. Otherwise, you risk a significant loss of sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T23:18:07-07:00","id":1406068,"title":"","content":"In previous Mage supplements they talk about different &quot;videres&quot; that distinguish between the three umbras. In pseudo-scientific speak of &quot;real&quot; occult, they'd probably refer to these as different &quot;vibrations&quot;.<br /> <br /> In terms of most practical applications, these are three separate experiences. For the purposes of that quote of Mage, they are simply dividing reality into two layers - the material and the spiritual. But these does not mean each &quot;layer&quot; of the umbra takes place all together. Wraiths/Spectres/Plasmic creatures do not interact with Gaian spirits/Garou/Banes or Astral Umbrood. But some spirits probably do perceive and interact with multiple layers of reality.<br /> <br /> If one Mage perceives one reality, they likely do not perceive the others. If they do perceive more than one umbra, I would simply describe each layers by itself. What someone sees at one &quot;layer&quot; may not exist at all on another &quot;layer&quot;. Only a very few spirits would manifest on more than one layer at a given time.<br /> <br /> And once a Mage leaves the Penumbra, there is likely little crossover. Someone going into the Tempest does not have a corresponding section in Astral or Gaian.<br /> <br /> However, there are places in these umbras that are in &quot;flux&quot; meaning it is possible to crossover from one &quot;layer&quot; to another. As you said, the Book of Worlds does detail where some of these fluxes exist.<br /> <br /> From a practical point of view for an ST, I would say to describe each of these layers as separate, but that there are sections where it is possible to cross over from one to another. And that the Penumbras of each, since each is located on the material world, is one of those places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:36:03-07:00","id":1406097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405871-mages-and-the-penumbra-s?p=1406029#post1406029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>The books you mention are a good read for Mage's version of the Umbra, but don't clarify much about the subject you've brought<br /> <br /> A suggestion: If 3 wizards go to the Penumbra, either there's a &quot;lead&quot; and the rest follow into their Videre OR there's a combination of the appropiate videres in a single landscape. That way you don't need to narrate 3 different landscapes, one for each wizard (I think this much is suggested in one of these books, I'm not sure tho)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T09:20:34-07:00","id":1406282,"title":"","content":"Ive been thinking about dividing my Penumbra in &quot;patches&quot;. Every single penumbral place would be aligned to either the High, Middle or Low Umbra. Some of them would have portals connecting to deeper realms inside those Umbras (astral realms, werewolf realms, and stygia or whatever it is beyond the shadowlands).<br /> <br /> For example, a University with a Penumbra associated to the High Umbra, this Park with one associated to the Middle Umbra, and this Graveyard or Haunted house associated to the Low Umbra. That way I wouldnt be describing things different or thinking about layers and layers of spiritual reality. <br /> <br /> I'll check the book of worlds to see if the vision exposed there works better, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T00:40:21-07:00","id":1406395,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s one way that you could theoretically go about it, particularly in parts of the Penumbra that are close to the periphery.<br /> <br /> [3 Awakened - a geomancer, spirit medium, and apocalyptic prophet step into the penumbra of a city park. The park is circular, boasts a well manicured lawn and a few trees, and at the center has a statue of a notable local figure standing on a stone plinth. The plinth also holds an informative plaque.]<br /> <br /> \u2022The Geomancer (Higher Lenses)<br /> The Geomancer enters a perfectly aligned circular clearing surrounded by gates forming perfect curves. They see a precise number of trees and the way that their roots and branches form precise symmetries. They see the pathways that energy takes as it descends from the Primium and follows channels into and through the earth - outward and upward. They see the grass forming perfect blades in fractal growth patterns. They see a shining statue of a great man whose pedestal calmly but proudly lists out the many great deeds of his life and why he is deserving of the energy and recognition he receives in his prized place here.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Spirit Medium (Middle Lenses)<br /> The Spirit Medium enters a clearing that forms a clear circle with tall metallic barriers that stand as sentries. They see a scattering of trees, old and powerful, but slowly fading away and being replaced by trees that are \u2018cleaner\u2019 and \u2018obedient\u2019. They may even see spider webbing in the branches of these trees. They see spirits - gafflings and englings- flitting about amongst the grasses and feeding the greater spirits of the trees and beasts, all under the watchful eye of the celestines above. They see tall grasses constantly being cut away by spirits of order, gardeners forcing the landscape into a certain fashion. The spirits are adapting, if begrudgingly, as they see the pavement nearby and know that there are worse fates. They see a proud man stood upon a platform, staring down at his new domain. His admirers have granted him this place and if the trees or grass argue his gardeners cowe them. If asked he will proudly explain why it is his right to call this place his and at a gesture this nascent jaggling can have any of his spiritual followers provide him the resources he needs to grow even stronger. So long as his liege, the local City Mother, remains pleased with him he will go far.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Apocalyptic Prophet (Lower Lenses)<br /> The Apocalyptic Prophet enters through rusting gates and sees the slow corrosion of their hinges as they step into the circular park. They see the many stumps and a few have shadowy trees yet but most are rotting markers of the trees that once grew here, and the few trees that remain. They are faint now, but the prophet can already see the marks of rot in a few and the stunting of growth that will slowly see them fade away. They see how much grass is destroyed to feed the ground, animals, and trees. They see the chemicals which are slowing decomposition and how the grass is growing fainter. They see shimmers of the tall grasses that once were, but they are vague and inconstant - almost forgotten. They see a cracked pedestal and a statue of a man that is still recognizable. This will not last - the prophet knows that time will rub the man\u2019s features away until all that remains will be a dull caricature - a life only remembered as a name and a few dry facts and anecdotes. The prophet looks down and sees another possibility though. Black ooze flows down from behind the plaque that bluntly reads out the man\u2019s achievements. The prophet recognizes the signs of dark secrets and smiles wryly. Should they ever be learned, the statue will ooze tar forevermore. All features covered by the sickness of his own misdeeds. The man stares down at the prophet, uneasy. He answers honestly about questions regarding public knowledge but says no more. He fears the prophet and what they may discover. He should.<br /> <br /> (These are three ways of describing the exact same space, information, and avenues that a player could use to interact with a setting or gain inspiration. The only differences are the methods, flavors, paradigm, and - most importantly - perspectives. I hope that these three examples were useful.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T03:47:13-07:00","id":1406408,"title":"","content":"Note: it's the same <i>landscape</i> in all three cases, albeit with different appearances based on the observer. Everything that one of them sees, the others see as well. But their different perceptions emphasize different aspects of the scene. <br /> <br /> But more importantly, the denizens that each encounters are not part of the landscape, and will be different. There will be Astral entities, nature spirits, and ghosts present; the geomancer will interact with the Astral entities, the spirit medium will interact with the nature spirits, and the Apocalyptic prophet will interact with the ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}